  "result": "Fixed. `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py` moved the wrong way for open bounds, so clamping fell outside the range.\n\n- **Cause:** it returned `bound - dir`. With `min_open=True`, a value below the minimum clamped to `min - 1`, still out of range. With `max_open=True` it clamped to `max + 1`.\n- **Fix:** it now returns `bound + dir`, giving `min + 1` and `max - 1` respectively. Closed bounds were already correct and are unchanged.\n- **Tests:** I added two cases to `tests/test_types.py`, a `min_open` clamp (`-1` \u2192 `1`) and a `max_open` clamp (`9` \u2192 `4`). `tests/test_types.py` passes (43 passed, 2 skipped); I did not run the full suite.",
